Copy the image sidecars from the default options

qtcReadConfig builds the default options, which hold the values of the
system configuration file, and copies one field of them into the target.
The two pixmap sidecars stay behind. An absent appearance key makes
toAppearance answer the default appearance and leave the pixmap alone.
An inherited appearance of APPEARANCE_FILE therefore reaches the style
with a null pixmap. QPainter drops a null tile, and the window
background or the menu background never paints its image.

Copy bgndPixmap and menuBgndPixmap beside customGradient. A file that
names its own image still loads that image, because the file branch of
toAppearance writes both the path and the pixmap.

The change sits on the branch work/config-io of the local tree, as commit 15 of 18.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/qt6/common/config_file.cpp b/qt6/common/config_file.cpp
index 855c4136..d0d8ce01 100644
--- a/qt6/common/config_file.cpp
+++ b/qt6/common/config_file.cpp
@@ -1255,7 +1255,13 @@ bool qtcReadConfig(const QString &file, Options *opts, Options *defOpts, bool ch
             Options *def=&newOpts;
 
             if(opts!=def)
+            {
                 opts->customGradient=def->customGradient;
+                /* The appearance readers leave a pixmap alone when the key is
+                   absent, so an inherited image appearance needs its image. */
+                opts->bgndPixmap=def->bgndPixmap;
+                opts->menuBgndPixmap=def->menuBgndPixmap;
+            }
             /* Check if the config file expects old default values... */
             if(opts->version<qtcMakeVersion(1, 6))
             {
